00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:07,640
The technical execution is fully commoditized.

190
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:09,920
So what makes a photograph valuable today?

191
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:10,920
The human element.

192
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:11,920
Exactly.

193
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:12,920
It's not the exposure.

194
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:13,920
It's the human taste.

195
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:18,080
It's the eye for composition, the emotional timing, the creative vision.

196
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:19,600
Tomorrow is human.

197
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:23,880
The more automated our tools get, the more our human taste is our only differentiator.

198
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:25,320
That is a great way to put it.

199
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:29,920
The challenge is that AI models by their mathematical nature have terrible taste.

200
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:30,920
Really?

201
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:31,920
Terrible taste.

202
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:32,920
Yeah.

203
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:37,040
Because they are designed to minimize loss and optimize for human preference during training,

204
00:09:37,040 --> 00:09:39,520
