00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:47,160
They regress to the mean.

208
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:48,160
Oh right.

209
00:09:48,160 --> 00:09:51,280
So they write boring middle of the road corporate speak.

210
00:09:51,280 --> 00:09:52,280
Always.

211
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:57,440
Therefore, human-to-human collaboration and friction become more vital, not less.

212
00:09:57,440 --> 00:10:01,520
You don't get exceptional output by having a single human type of prompt into an empty

213
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:02,880
text box.

214
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:08,000
The vibe-teaming method, detailed by Brookings, relies on seating the AI with highly divergent

215
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
human context.

216
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:12,840
So you feed it the messy, brilliant arguments between human experts?

217
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:17,280
You capture the transcription of a passionate, hour-long debate between experts who vehemently

218
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:19,200
disagree on a policy approach.

219
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:21,200
You feed that raw friction into the model.

220
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,200
Oh, that's smart.

221
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:23,200
Right.

222
00:10:23,200 --> 00:10:28,280
That forces the AI to navigate the contours of a complex edge case problem, rather than

223
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:31,400
defaulting to a Wikipedia-style summary.

